Implemented Vercel Web Analytics for Next.js App Router

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package (version 1.5.0)
- Updated package.json with the new dependency
- Generated updated package-lock.json

### 2. Analytics Configuration (app/layout.tsx)
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/next';`
- Integrated the `<Analytics />` component inside the body element of the root layout
- Preserved existing layout structure, fonts, and styling

## Modified Files
- `app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree

## Implementation Details
The Analytics component was added according to the official Vercel documentation:
- Placed within the body element for proper tracking
- Uses the Next.js-specific import path (`@vercel/analytics/next`)
- Will automatically track page views and visitor analytics once deployed to Vercel

## Verification
✓ Build completed successfully (npm run build)
✓ TypeScript compilation passed
✓ No changes to existing functionality
✓ Package lock file properly updated

